/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Ethanol-water bubble temperature at 101.325 kPa -- THE FITTED SUBSET.

  Provenance: transcribed from constant/experiments/ethanol-water-101kPa of
  tutorials/steady/optimisation/fitNRTL01_ethanol_water, which records its own
  source as DECHEMA / Gmehling-Onken Vol. I Part 1, pedagogical subset.  These
  are MEASURED data, not generated -- which is what makes the held-out test in
  this case a statement about the model rather than about arithmetic.

  THE SPLIT IS DECLARED, AND IT IS ARITHMETIC.  Every THIRD point of the
  eleven-point series (the 3rd, 6th and 9th, i.e. x1 = 0.20, 0.50, 0.80) is
  held out; the remaining eight are here.  The rule was written down before
  anything was fitted and does not look at a single residual.  It spreads the
  held-out points across the composition range rather than cutting the series
  in half, because a model can extrapolate badly and interpolate well, and a
  contiguous cut would test only one of those.

  Licence: GPL-3.0-or-later.  The numbers are a small pedagogical subset
  transcribed within the corpus, carried here unchanged from the case that
  already ships them.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

columns
(
    { name x1;  unit -;  }     // liquid mole fraction of ethanol
    { name T;   unit K;  }     // bubble temperature at 101.325 kPa
);

data
(
    0.05  361.95
    0.10  359.95
    0.30  357.30
    0.40  356.85
    0.60  355.30
    0.70  354.50
    0.90  351.85
    0.95  351.45
);
